- The index is between 0 and the size of the list inclusive.
- For every valid index from this index to the old size of the list, the element at the next position is either null and the old element at this index is null, or the element at the next position equals the old element at this index.

Given these conditions, we can construct the assert statement using the provided syntax and rules. Here's how we can express it:

1. We need to check the condition for every valid index from `index` to `\old(this.size())`.
2. For each of these indices, we need to check if the element at the next position is either null and the old element at this index is null, or the element at the next position equals the old element at this index.

The assert statement can be written as follows:

<code>assert \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); (this.get(i + 1) == null && \old(this.get(i)) == null) || this.get(i + 1) == \old(this.get(i));</code>

